Abstract:
Under certain conditions the state space of a discrete time Markov chain (DTMC) can be partitioned into subsets of states called lumpings, each of which can be treated as a single state of a smaller Markov chain. Such a chain is said to be “lumpable” and this article provides an overview of the conditions and methods for examining aggregated chains for lumpability. 


Keywords: 

lumpability; 
state aggregation; 
Markov chains; 
merged states; 
aggregation
